<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L3_3_1_3" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L3_3_1_3">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L3_3_1_3" name="3.1.3 Grinding &amp; Classification" processRef="Process_L3_3_1_3"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L3_3_1_3" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L0/L1/L2 Process. SAG and ball mills reduce ore to the target grind size (P80 75–150 µm) in a wet grinding circuit with water addition and steel grinding media. Hydrocyclone clusters classify ground slurry — underflow (coarse) is recycled to the ball mill, overflow (fine) advances to flotation as the mill circuit product. The mill circuit product P80 is the key quality handoff from Comminution to Flotation.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L3_3_1_3">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_1_3_dcs" name="Control Room Operator / DCS Auto-control">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_1_3_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_1_3_g1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_1_3_n1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_1_3_g2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_1_3_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_1_3_met" name="Metallurgist / Plant Operator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_1_3_n2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_1_3_s2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_1_3_e2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_1_3_s" name="COS reclaim feeding SAG mill">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_1" name="3.1.3.1 Operate SAG Mill">
      <bpmn:documentation>Semi-autogenous grinding (SAG) mill uses ore itself as the primary grinding medium, supplemented by a charge of steel balls (typically 10–15% v/v). DCS controls mill speed (% critical), bearing pressure (proxy for mill load/charge mass), water addition rate, and feed rate. SAG mill power draw is the primary throughput optimisation variable. Mill discharge passes through a discharge screen — pebbles are diverted to pebble crushing; undersize advances to the ball mill. [P754: mass flow (indirect — via feed belt weigher and water flow meter) | belt weigher + flow meter | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 2 | NO — internal process node]
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Control Room Operator
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: sag_mill_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g1" name="Excess pebbles?" default="Flow_L3_3_1_3_4">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_1_3_n1" name="Divert pebbles to pebble crusher">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition). Pebble crushing is 3.1.2.3 (Cu sites only); crushed pebbles return to the SAG mill.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_2" name="3.1.3.2 Operate Ball Mill">
      <bpmn:documentation>Ball mill(s) receive SAG mill undersize discharge (or primary crushed ore at Red Dog three-stage circuit) and grind to the target cyclone feed size using a steel ball charge. DCS controls ball mill speed, water addition, and feed rate. Ball mill power draw is monitored continuously. Sump level (cyclone feed sump) is controlled by variable-speed pump. [P754: mass flow (indirect — via cyclone feed density and flow meter) | nuclear density gauge + magnetic flow meter | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 2 | NO — internal process node]
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Control Room Operator
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: ball_mill_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_3" name="3.1.3.3 Classify Slurry by Hydrocyclone">
      <bpmn:documentation>Hydrocyclone cluster(s) classify ball mill discharge slurry by particle size using centrifugal force. Cyclone overflow (fine fraction, P80 target met) advances to flotation conditioning as the mill circuit product — this is the Comminution-to-Flotation handoff. Cyclone underflow (coarse fraction) recirculates to the ball mill. Cyclone feed density and flow rate are monitored; overflow particle size is measured periodically (sieve analysis) or continuously (online PSA). [P754: grade (particle size proxy via density) | nuclear density gauge + periodic PSA | continuous density / periodic size | Principles 1, 2, 7 | NO — internal process classification node]
ISA-95 level: 2 / 1
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Control Room Operator
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 7
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (process_measurement_point — mill_circuit_product_p80)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g2" name="Cyclone overflow P80 on target?" default="Flow_L3_3_1_3_8">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_8</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_1_3_e" name="Cyclone overflow to flotation">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_8</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_1_3_n2" name="Adjust cyclone apex, feed density or throughput">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_1_3_s2" name="Ball addition interval reached">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_4" name="3.1.3.4 Manage Grinding Media Addition">
      <bpmn:documentation>Steel grinding balls are added to the SAG and ball mills at a controlled rate (t/hr of balls per t/hr of ore processed) to maintain the target ball charge volume and composition. Grinding media consumption is tracked by ball addition count (ball counter or weigh hopper) and is a significant reagent cost input to the processing cost model. Ball addition events are recorded per mill per shift.
ISA-95 level: 3
Actors: Metallurgist; Plant Operator
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Level 3 (inventory management); AMIRA P754 Principle 1 (mass of grinding media is an input to mass balance)
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (reagent_consumption_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_3_12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_1_3_e2" name="Grinding media added">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_3_12</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_1" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_1_3_s" targetRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_2" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_1" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_3" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g1" targetRef="Task_L3_3_1_3_n1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_4" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g1" targetRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_5" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_1_3_n1" targetRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_6" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_2" targetRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_7" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_3" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_8" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g2" targetRef="End_L3_3_1_3_e"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_9" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_1_3_g2" targetRef="Task_L3_3_1_3_n2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_10" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_1_3_n2" targetRef="Service_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_11" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_1_3_s2" targetRef="Task_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_3_12" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_1_3_3_1_3_4" targetRef="End_L3_3_1_3_e2"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L3_3_1_3">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L3_3_1_3" bpmnElement="Collab_L3_3_1_3">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L3_3_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L3_3_1_3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="1328" height="510"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
